# ArionComply sweep scheduler — cron recipe (Wave 3b, 2026-07-13)
#
# Runs one sweep tick every 30 minutes. Adjust the cadence to fit
# tenant volume. Each invocation is stateless — missed ticks just
# delay the next work item; nothing corrupts.
#
# Install:
#     sudo -u arionlabs crontab -e
#     # paste this file's contents (adjust paths)
#
# Or use system cron:
#     sudo cp deploy/scheduler.cron /etc/cron.d/arioncomply-scheduler
#
# Environment for python -m rag.scheduler:
#     PGHOST, PGDATABASE, PGUSER, PGPASSWORD  — reads from .env, or
#     override via the cron environment below.

# Every 30 minutes on the hour + half-hour, at any hour of any day
*/30 * * * *  cd /data/arioncomply && PYTHONPATH=/data/arioncomply /usr/bin/python3 -m rag.scheduler.tick >> /var/log/arioncomply/scheduler.log 2>&1

# Alternative cadences to consider:
# */5  * * * *   — every 5 minutes (aggressive; use if fact-refresh feels slow)
# 0    * * * *   — hourly on the hour
# 0    */6 * * * — every 6 hours (light touch — fine for stable tenant profiles)
